{
  "name": "customer",
  "main": "./src/index.ts",
  "compatibility_date": "2025-04-01",
  // `unsafe-eval` is required by `packages/schema-registry`, and **the test suite
  // cannot catch its absence**. `ajv.compile()` builds a validator with
  // `new Function()`, which Node permits and Workers forbids: `validate()` passes
  // under Vitest and throws `EvalError: Code generation from strings disallowed for
  // this context` once deployed.
  //
  // What that cost in production: `PUT /v1/customers` inserts the customer and only
  // then compiles the schema, so every new customer received `500 INTERNAL_ERROR`
  // **while the row was already committed**. They were registered and told they had
  // not been. A retry took the upsert branch and succeeded, which made a total outage
  // read as a flake — the failure that hid it for as long as it did.
  //
  // The flag costs exactly what it says: this worker can now generate code from
  // strings at runtime, and it holds customer PII. That was traded deliberately to
  // stop blocking registrations, and it is the first thing to revisit. The
  // alternatives are precompiling the schemas at build time — impossible while they
  // live in KV — or dropping runtime validation of the payload this same handler has
  // just constructed from its own typed insert.
  //
  // Removing this flag silently reintroduces the outage. Nothing fails: the tests are
  // green either way.
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat", "unsafe-eval"],
  "vars": {},
  "kv_namespaces": [
    {
      "binding": "SCHEMA_REGISTRY",
      "id": "732ccde5b0944db082d07667aba8104b"
    }
  ],
  "queues": {
    "producers": [
      {
        "binding": "DOMAIN_EVENTS_QUEUE",
        "queue": "vyloop-domain-events"
      }
    ]
  }
}
